  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Testing Your Types",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Example: Test Your Types",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "import { expectTypeOf } from 'vitest';",
            "expectTypeOf(getProp({ a: 1 }, 'a'))",
            "  .toEqualTypeOf<number>();",
            "expectTypeOf<Simplify<A & B>>()",
            "  .toEqualTypeOf<{ a: 1; b: 2 }>();"
          ],
          "note": "type-level code needs tests too"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Pitfalls to Avoid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Over-generic: five type params nobody can read",
            "`return {} as T` hides a real bug",
            "`new T()` or `typeof T` fails: T is erased",
            "`Object.keys` gives `string[]`, not `(keyof T)[]`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Generics vs Alternatives",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Use when"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Overloads",
              "clean per-case signatures"
            ],
            [
              "Generic + conditional",
              "one signature, weaker body check"
            ],
            [
              "`unknown`",
              "value is only passed around"
            ],
            [
              "Generic `T`",
              "output depends on input"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Simplify<T> =",
            "  { [K in keyof T]: T[K] } & {};",
            "type X = Simplify<{ a: 1 } & { b: 2 }>;",
            "// hover shows { a: 1; b: 2 }"
          ],
          "note": "flattens unreadable intersections"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Lint rule",
          "text": "`no-unnecessary-type-parameters` flags a type parameter that appears only once."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Unnecessary Generic",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function log<T>(x: T): void {}",
            "// same as:",
            "function log(x: unknown): void {}"
          ],
          "note": "T appears once: drop it"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Recursion Limits",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deep recursion gives \"excessively deep and possibly infinite\"",
            "Plain recursion bails out near ==50 levels==",
            "Tail-recursive conditionals reach about **1000**",
            "Use an accumulator param to make it tail-recursive"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Compile-Time Cost",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Slow `tsc`",
              "measure with `--generateTrace`"
            ],
            [
              "Laggy editor",
              "simplify conditional types"
            ],
            [
              "Unreadable errors",
              "wrap in `Simplify<T>`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Cast at the Boundary",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "const raw = JSON.parse(text);",
            "const cfg = raw as Config;",
            "// one cast, at the edge"
          ],
          "note": "cast at one small boundary"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`JSON.parse` and `Object.entries` lose generics",
            "Keep the **cast** in one small helper",
            "Pass a constructor or tag for runtime `T`"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "typescript",
      "subtitle": "Trade-offs in generics"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cheatsheet: Generics at a Glance",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Declare and Bound",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Syntax"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Generic function",
              "`function f<T>(x: T): T`"
            ],
            [
              "Constraint",
              "`<T extends { id: string }>`"
            ],
            [
              "Key lookup",
              "`<T, K extends keyof T>(o: T, k: K): T[K]`"
            ],
            [
              "Default",
              "`<T = unknown>`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function f<T>(x: T): T { return x }",
            "function id<T extends {id:string}>",
            "  (x: T) { return x.id }",
            "function get<T, K extends keyof T>",
            "  (o: T, k: K): T[K] {",
            "  return o[k] }"
          ],
          "note": "K must be a key of T"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Conditional and infer",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`T extends U ? X : Y` picks a branch at type level",
            "==Distributes== over unions when `T` is **naked**",
            "Wrap as `[T] extends [U]` to stop distribution",
            "`infer` captures a piece inside the extends clause"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Ret<T> =",
            "  T extends (...a: any[]) => infer R",
            "    ? R : never;",
            "type A = Ret<() => number>; // number"
          ],
          "note": "infer only inside extends"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Mapped Types",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Req<T> = {",
            "  -readonly [K in keyof T]-?: T[K]",
            "};",
            "type Get<T> = { [K in keyof T as",
            "  `get${Capitalize<K & string>}`]: T[K] };"
          ],
          "note": "as remaps key names"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Utility Table",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Utility",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Partial / Required / Readonly",
              "all keys ?, -?, readonly"
            ],
            [
              "Pick / Omit / Record",
              "keep, drop, build keys"
            ],
            [
              "ReturnType / Parameters / Awaited",
              "unwrap fn or Promise"
            ],
            [
              "NonNullable / Exclude / Extract",
              "filter union members"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Variance and Inference",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Annotation",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`out T`",
              "covariant (producer)"
            ],
            [
              "`in T`",
              "contravariant (consumer)"
            ],
            [
              "`in out T`",
              "invariant (read + write)"
            ],
            [
              "`NoInfer<T>` (TS 5.4)",
              "blocks a site as inference source"
            ],
            [
              "`const T` (TS 5.0)",
              "infers literal, readonly types"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Debug trick",
          "text": "Wrap a type in `Simplify<T>`, or hover over a type alias, to see the expanded shape."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Summary",
          "text": "Generics link types, constraints bound them, keyof and indexed access index them, conditional and mapped types transform them."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "react",
